# CODEOWNERS — automatic reviewer assignment (Issue #1815)
#
# GitHub requests a review from the matching owner whenever a pull request
# touches a path below. Without this, review requests are assigned by hand and
# a change to an area can be merged without anyone who knows that area seeing
# it.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom and **the last match wins** — not the most
# specific one. So the catch-all goes first and the narrow paths after it,
# which is the opposite of how .gitignore reads.
#
# Owners must have write access to the repository, or GitHub silently skips the
# rule rather than reporting an error. If a review is not being requested for an
# area, that is the first thing to check.
#
# Replace the placeholder teams below with real teams or usernames before
# merging — a CODEOWNERS file naming a team that does not exist assigns nothing
# and is worse than none, because the repository looks covered.

# ─── Default ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything not matched by a rule further down.
*                           @Web3Novalabs/maintainers

# ─── Soroban contract ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On-chain code: a mistake here is immutable once deployed and can move funds.
/contract/                  @Web3Novalabs/contract-reviewers

# ─── Rust backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/backend/                   @Web3Novalabs/backend-reviewers

# ─── Next.js frontend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/frontend/                  @Web3Novalabs/frontend-reviewers

# ─── Infrastructure ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Terraform and Docker: changes here affect every environment at once.
/terraform/                 @Web3Novalabs/infra-reviewers
/docker/                    @Web3Novalabs/infra-reviewers
/docker-compose.yml         @Web3Novalabs/infra-reviewers

# ─── Repository automation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Workflows, templates, and this file. A change to CI can disable the checks
# protecting everything above, so it is owned by maintainers rather than by the
# area whose workflow is being edited.
/.github/                   @Web3Novalabs/maintainers

# ─── Security policy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/SECURITY.md                @Web3Novalabs/maintainers
